{
  "_readme": [
    "Bible book names in Relay's tier-1 languages, keyed by the canonical English",
    "name in detection::CANONICAL_BOOKS.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS DATA AND NOT RUST:",
    "Relay's differentiator is African-language speech. Its maintainer does not",
    "speak all three of these languages fluently, and a WRONG alias does not fail",
    "safely — it puts the wrong scripture on a wall in front of a congregation.",
    "Keeping the names here means a native speaker can correct them in a one-line",
    "pull request without touching Rust, without a build, and without knowing what",
    "a HashMap is. That is the only way this table ever becomes trustworthy.",
    "",
    "MULTIPLE TRANSLATIONS PER LANGUAGE. Yorùbá is the clearest case: Biblica's",
    "Yoruba Contemporary Bible calls Psalms 'Sáàmù', while the older Bibeli Mímọ́",
    "calls it 'Psalmu'. A preacher says whatever their own Bible says, so BOTH are",
    "listed. Add more; there is no cost to an extra alias that is correct.",
    "",
    "MATCHING IS DIACRITIC-INSENSITIVE. 'Jòhánù', 'Johánù' and 'Johanu' all match:",
    "detection::normalize folds tone marks, dots-below and the Hausa hooked letters",
    "(ɓ ɗ ƙ ƴ) before lookup, because whisper emits all of these spellings depending",
    "on the audio. Write the name properly — the folding is handled for you.",
    "",
    "WORDS THAT ARE ALSO ORDINARY WORDS ARE DELIBERATELY OMITTED.",
    "Yorùbá 'Iṣẹ́' (Acts) also just means 'work'. 'Orin' (Song of Solomon) also just",
    "means 'song' — in a church. Listing those bare would fire scripture off normal",
    "speech, so only the full forms ('Ìṣe àwọn Àpọ́sítélì', 'Orin Solomoni') are here.",
    "If you add a name, ask first: could a preacher say this word WITHOUT meaning the",
    "book?",
    "",
    "OMISSION IS SAFE. A missing alias just means Relay does not detect that book in",
    "that language yet. A WRONG alias means a wrong verse on the screen. If you are",
    "not sure, leave it out and say so — someone who is sure will add it.",
    "",
    "Sources — Swahili: Biblia Takatifu / Neno (Biblica). Yorùbá: Yoruba",
    "Contemporary Bible (Biblica) + Bibeli Mímọ́. Hausa: Bible Society of Nigeria",
    "1932/2010 + Hausa Contemporary Bible (Biblica).",
    "",
    "STATUS: all three languages complete (66/66). Reviewed against published",
    "translations, but NOT yet by a native speaker of Yorùbá or Hausa — see",
    "docs/LANGUAGES.md. Corrections very welcome."
  ],

